        "---\n",
        "## Part 1: The 5G gNodeB Context Table (3GPP TS 38.331)\n",
        "In 5G, when a phone wants to connect, it sends an initial request (**Msg3**).\n",
       
        "First we will define 5G cell tower with a capacity of **16 users**:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "CellTower class defined successfully!\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "class CellTower:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, max_capacity=16, timer_seconds=2.7):\n",
        "        self.max_capacity = max_capacity   # Maximum concurrent connection slots\n",
        "        self.timer = timer_seconds         # Waiting timer (T300 = 2.7s)\n",
        "        self.contexts = {}                 # Stores active users: {user_id: expiry_time}\n",
        "        \n",
        "    def purge_expired(self, current_time):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Free up slots if 2.7s passed without completion\"\"\"\n",
        "        for uid, expiry in list(self.contexts.items()):\n",
        "            if current_time >= expiry:\n",
        "                del self.contexts[uid]\n",
        "                \n",
        "    def handle_msg3(self, user_id, current_time):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Handle incoming connection request (Msg3)\"\"\"\n",
        "        self.purge_expired(current_time)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # If memory table is completely full, reject request\n",
        "        if len(self.contexts) >= self.max_capacity:\n",
        "            return False  # REJECTED (Out of memory!)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Allocate context slot\n",
        "        self.contexts[user_id] = current_time + self.timer\n",
        "        return True       # ALLOCATED\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"CellTower class defined successfully!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Run The First Attack: Context Exhaustion\n",
        "An attacker floods the tower with **45.7 requests/second** and never completes connection.\n",
        "The 16 slots will fill up!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "--- Starting Flood ---\n",
            "[   0.0 ms] Req # 1: ADMITTED (Occupied: 1/16)\n",
            "[  21.9 ms] Req # 2: ADMITTED (Occupied: 2/16)\n",
            "[  43.8 ms] Req # 3: ADMITTED (Occupied: 3/16)\n",
            "[  65.6 ms] Req # 4: ADMITTED (Occupied: 4/16)\n",
            "[  87.5 ms] Req # 5: ADMITTED (Occupied: 5/16)\n",
            "[ 109.4 ms] Req # 6: ADMITTED (Occupied: 6/16)\n",
            "[ 131.3 ms] Req # 7: ADMITTED (Occupied: 7/16)\n",
            "[ 153.2 ms] Req # 8: ADMITTED (Occupied: 8/16)\n",
            "[ 175.1 ms] Req # 9: ADMITTED (Occupied: 9/16)\n",
            "[ 196.9 ms] Req #10: ADMITTED (Occupied: 10/16)\n",
            "[ 218.8 ms] Req #11: ADMITTED (Occupied: 11/16)\n",
            "[ 240.7 ms] Req #12: ADMITTED (Occupied: 12/16)\n",
            "[ 262.6 ms] Req #13: ADMITTED (Occupied: 13/16)\n",
            "[ 284.5 ms] Req #14: ADMITTED (Occupied: 14/16)\n",
            "[ 306.3 ms] Req #15: ADMITTED (Occupied: 15/16)\n",
            "[ 328.2 ms] Req #16: ADMITTED (Occupied: 16/16)\n",
            "[ 350.1 ms] Req #17: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\n",
            "[ 372.0 ms] Req #18: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\n",
            "[ 393.9 ms] Req #19: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\n",
            "[ 415.8 ms] Req #20: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\n",
            "[ 437.6 ms] Req #21: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\n",
            "----------------------\n",
            "Our Simulated Depletion Time: 328.2 ms\n",
            "StormShield Paper Result (Fig 6): 318 ms\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "tower = CellTower(max_capacity=16)\n",
        "rate = 45.7                        # 45.7 Msg3/s (from StormShield paper)\n",
        "interval = 1.0 / rate              # about 22 ms between requests\n",
        "\n",
        "current_time = 0.0\n",
        "depletion_time = None\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"--- Starting Flood ---\")\n",
        "for req_num in range(1, 22):\n",
        "    user_id = f\"Attacker_UE_{req_num}\"\n",
        "    admitted = tower.handle_msg3(user_id, current_time)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if admitted:\n",
        "        print(f\"[{current_time*1000:6.1f} ms] Req #{req_num:2d}: ADMITTED (Occupied: {len(tower.contexts)}/16)\")\n",
        "        if len(tower.contexts) == 16 and depletion_time is None:\n",
        "            depletion_time = current_time\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(f\"[{current_time*1000:6.1f} ms] Req #{req_num:2d}: BLOCKED! Table is 100% EXHAUSTED!\")\n",
        "        \n",
        "    current_time += interval\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"----------------------\")\n",
        "print(f\"Our Simulated Depletion Time: {depletion_time*1000:.1f} ms\")\n",
        "print(\"StormShield Paper Result (Fig 6): 318 ms\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 2: Reproducing Figure 6 Across Capacities (16, 32, 48, 64)\n",
        "In Figure 6 of the paper, the authors tested what happens if the cell tower is upgraded to allow **16, 32, 48, or 64 users**.\n"
        
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Capacity 16 UEs -> Paper:  318 ms | Simulated:  328.2 ms | Error:  3.2%\n",
            "Capacity 32 UEs -> Paper:  662 ms | Simulated:  678.3 ms | Error:  2.5%\n",
            "Capacity 48 UEs -> Paper: 1164 ms | Simulated: 1028.4 ms | Error: 11.6%\n",
            "Capacity 64 UEs -> Paper: 1486 ms | Simulated: 1378.6 ms | Error:  7.2%\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 700x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "capacities = [16, 32, 48, 64]\n",
        "paper_times = [318, 662, 1164, 1486]  # Exact numbers from StormShield Figure 6\n",
        "simulated_times = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for cap in capacities:\n",
        "    test_tower = CellTower(max_capacity=cap)\n",
        "    t = 0.0\n",
        "    dep_t = None\n",
        "    req_id = 1\n",
        "    while t < 5.0:\n",
        "        success = test_tower.handle_msg3(f\"Atk_{req_id}\", t)\n",
        "        if len(test_tower.contexts) == cap and dep_t is None:\n",
        "            dep_t = t\n",
        "            break\n",
        "        t += (1.0 / 45.7)\n",
        "        req_id += 1\n",
        "    simulated_times.append(dep_t * 1000.0) # in ms\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plotting side-by-side\n",
        "x = np.arange(len(capacities))\n",
        "width = 0.35\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
        "plt.bar(x - width/2, paper_times, width, label='StormShield Published (WiSec 2026)', color='#3366cc')\n",
        "plt.bar(x + width/2, simulated_times, width, label='Our Simulation (TS 38.331)', color='#dc3912')\n",
        "plt.xticks(x, capacities)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('gNB Max Context Capacity (UEs)')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Depletion Latency (ms)')\n",
        "plt.title('Reproduction of StormShield Figure 6: Context Depletion')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "for c, p, s in zip(capacities, paper_times, simulated_times):\n",
        "    err = abs(s - p) / p * 100\n",
        "    print(f\"Capacity {c:2d} UEs -> Paper: {p:4d} ms | Simulated: {s:6.1f} ms | Error: {err:4.1f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 3: Adding StormShield Defense (DBSCAN + Spatial Fingerprint)\n",
        "How does StormShield detect and stop this attack?\n",
        "1. **Signal Fingerprint:** Every phone transmission has two physical measurements:\n",
        "   - **Timing Advance (TA):** Coarse distance to tower (integer index 0 to 63).\n",
        "   - **Signal Strength (RSSI):** Power in dBm (e.g. -65 dBm or -75 dBm).\n",
        "2. **Clustering:** An attacker transmitting from one spot will produce requests that cluster around the same $ point.\n",
        "3. **Radius ($\\epsilon_{\text{RSSI}}$):** StormShield sets this boundary to **\text{ dB}*.\n"
        
        
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Detected Attacker Cluster Size: 20 requests\n",
            "Calculated Malicious Centroid : TA = 2.0, RSSI = -64.97 dBm\n",
            "Action -> Centroid is added to the BLOCKLIST!\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN\n",
        "import random\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate 20 fake requests from an attacker at TA=2, RSSI=-65 dBm (with random channel noise)\n",
        "random.seed(42)\n",
        "attacker_samples = []\n",
        "for _ in range(20):\n",
        "    ta = 2.0\n",
        "    rssi = -65.0 + random.gauss(0, 1.2)  # Noise standard dev = 1.2 dB\n",
        "    attacker_samples.append([ta, rssi])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run DBSCAN with radius eps_rssi = 4 dB\n",
        "db = DBSCAN(eps=4.0, min_samples=3).fit(attacker_samples)\n",
        "labels = db.labels_\n",
        "\n",
        "# Find cluster centroid (the malicious fingerprint to block)\n",
        "pts = np.array(attacker_samples)\n",
        "malicious_cluster = pts[labels == 0]\n",
        "centroid = np.mean(malicious_cluster, axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Detected Attacker Cluster Size: {len(malicious_cluster)} requests\")\n",
        "print(f\"Calculated Malicious Centroid : TA = {centroid[0]:.1f}, RSSI = {centroid[1]:.2f} dBm\")\n",
        "print(f\"Action -> Centroid is added to the BLOCKLIST!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 4: The Vulnerability (Why StormShield Drops Innocent Users!)\n",
        
        "StormShield's radius is **fixed at \text{ dB}*.\n",
        "\n",
        "What happens if an innocent user is walking and their signal happens to be close to the attacker (e.g. at 569X68.5\text{ dBm}$, which is only .5\text{ dB}$ away)?\n",
        "The blocklist will mistakenly blocks the innocent user!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Error: unterminated string literal (detected at line 25) (<string>, line 25)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Centroid blocked by StormShield\n",
        "blocked_ta = centroid[0]\n",
        "blocked_rssi = centroid[1]\n",
        "fixed_radius = 4.0  # 4 dB fixed radius\n",
        "\n",
        "# Test innocent user at 3 different locations\n",
        "innocent_test_cases = [\n",
        "    (\"Location P1 (Close)\", 2.0, -68.5),   # 3.5 dB difference from attacker\n",
        "    (\"Location P3 (Medium)\", 2.0, -72.0),  # 7.0 dB difference from attacker\n",
        "    (\"Location P5 (Far)\", 2.0, -77.0)     # 12.0 dB difference from attacker\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"--- Testing Innocent User Against Fixed 4 dB Blocklist ---\")\n",
        "for name, u_ta, u_rssi in innocent_test_cases:\n",
        "    dist = abs(u_rssi - blocked_rssi)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # If inside 4 dB radius, StormShield blocks the innocent user!\n",
        "    if dist <= fixed_radius:\n",
        "        status = \"\u274c COLLATERAL BLOCKING! (Innocent user was BLOCKED!)\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        status = \"\u2705 ALLOWED (Connected successfully)\"\n",
        "        \n",
        "    print(f\"{name:<22}: RSSI={u_rssi:5.1f} dBm (Diff={dist:4.1f} dB) -> {status}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\n This reproduces why StormShield suffers a 17-25% Collateral Blocking Rate in Table 4!")
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Part 5: Plotting Table 4 & Figure 7 (Mobility & Collateral Blocking)\n",
        "In Table 4 and Figure 7 of StormShield, the authors showed that as a victim moves closer to the attacker,\n",
        "their connection success drops down to 60-70% and collateral blocking jumps to 17-25%.\n"
        
      ]
    },
